## Frequently Asked Questions

### Can I use Momo for my startup?

**No**, not under this license. Startup use is considered commercial. Contact us for commercial licensing.

### Can I use Momo in my university research project?

**Yes**, educational and research use is permitted under this license.

### Can I modify Momo and distribute my modified version?

**Yes**, for noncommercial purposes only. Your modified version must also be licensed under the same PolyForm Noncommercial License, and you must preserve attribution.

### Can a non-profit organization use Momo?

**Yes**, use by qualified non-profit organizations is permitted regardless of funding source.

### What happens if I violate the license?

You'll receive written notice and have 32 days to cure the violation. If you come into compliance within that period, your license continues. Otherwise, all licenses terminate immediately.

### Can I contribute to Momo under this license?

**Yes**, open source contributions are permitted and encouraged. See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for guidelines.

### How do I get a commercial license?

Contact us at licensing@holdtroop.dev with details about your use case, and we'll provide a quote for commercial licensing.

